    familyAdventure: "Do a Shadow Experiment together. Go outside three times in one day: morning, midday, and late afternoon. Each time, stand in the same spot and have someone trace your shadow with chalk on the sidewalk (or place a stick in the ground and mark the shadow tip). Compare: how did the shadow change? (Long in morning, short at midday, long and opposite direction in evening.) You just proved that Earth rotates! Nova the Owl would be impressed by your scientific observation.",
